   },
   "evidence": "In src/pipeline/lan-agent.ts:73-79 at head: `try { resume = open(job.state) && matches(request) && (await publication.resume(request)); } catch (error) { if (spec.signal.aborted) return cancelled(id); if (workers.agentJob(id)?.state === \"done\") continue; throw error; }`. When the job is still open, nothing cancels it before the error is rethrown. The engine's resume hook (engine.ts) turns any error from headSha, clean or privateEntries into a NeedsHumanError, so the run becomes needs_human. That status is terminal, so keptAgentJobs leaves the job out of the keep set and only the next start() or stop() cancels it. The request's case 5 requires an open job that fails reconciliation to be cancelled when it is open."
