  "id": "F2",
  "title": "The late result report must still stop on worker shutdown",
  "file": "src/workers/client.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker has pushed a commit while the coordinator is unreachable, and the owner (or launchd) stops the worker. The worker keeps retrying the result report until the job's attempt deadline, which can be many minutes, and shutdown waits for it, so the worker hangs instead of exiting.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: needs a full worker loop with an unreachable coordinator and a shutdown during the retry; the evidence below is quoted code",
   "evidence": "client.ts:857-862 at head: `call(`${path}/result`, report, sha === req.parentSha ? jobSignal : AbortSignal.timeout(Math.max(0, deadline - Date.now())))`. Only the deadline timeout bounds this signal; the worker-level `combined` signal (signal + stop.signal, line 459) is not part of it. `call` (lines 505-528) retries 5xx and network failures with `sleep(delay, \u2026, { signal: requestSignal })` until that signal aborts. The report closure is awaited inside the job task (withCheckout: `await report?.()`). Shutdown's finally block (around lines 984-990) runs `await Promise.allSettled([...allJobs().map(([, j]) => j.task), ...])`, so stopping the worker waits until the attempt deadline (up to timeoutMs + 360 s). The deadline bound matches the request; leaving out shutdown is the defect."
  },
  "B": {
